SHAPE RULE, measured by dd o-prime against dd main a53b79d and BINDING: rows do NOT nest inside rows. The shape is `section -> (optional dynamic-key map) -> row`. Recurse a section's value STRUCTURALLY and treat any object carrying a string `id` as a row; do NOT bound depth on a rule about rows and do NOT build a row-in-row parser — you would be modelling something that does not exist.
TREE: file Element (kind File) -> one Container per section -> one `ElementKind::Row` per id-bearing row, with the map key, where present, appearing in `trail` and in the address. A section with NO id-bearing rows becomes a single Section element, not a row set. The document is never the primary chunk.
ADDRESS: the positional dd form only — `file#section/id`, or `file#section/<key>/id` for a dynamic-key map. NEVER emit `file#id`: ids are document-unique but the grammar is positional and the short form does not resolve (dd measured E450).
EMBED TEXT (`raw_text`): schema-declared, never name-inferred. Fields declared `text` are embedded; fields declared `string` are embedded and marked lower-weight; `state`/`enum`/`int`/`number`/`bool`/`link` fields and raw ids are NEVER embedded. Prefix the parent trail so a row is findable by its document's subject matter. With `facts: None`, fall back to all JSON-string-valued fields except `id` and `state`, and set `EmbedBasis::Fallback`.
DISCOVERY: admit exact `.dd.json` BEFORE the config-format exclusion at crates/parsers/src/discovery.rs:720 — ordinary `.json` must still skip with `SkipReason::ConfigFormat`. Skip `.dd.md`. `dd.sweep_exclude` does NOT affect admission (dd's ruling: index it normally; the flag only excludes from corpus health reporting).
DO NOT TOUCH: `parsers::scan` (crates/parsers/src/lib.rs:111) keeps its exact existing signature — ddoc dispatch happens in the daemon, which is the only layer that can resolve a schema. Do not widen it.

```sql
-- crates/store/migrations/0014_ddoc_layer.sql — the only migration in this plan
ALTER TABLE elements DROP CONSTRAINT elements_kind_known;
ALTER TABLE elements ADD CONSTRAINT elements_kind_known
  CHECK (kind IN ('file','container','function','section','row'));
ALTER TABLE elements ADD COLUMN ddoc JSONB;          -- NULL for every code element
CREATE INDEX elements_ddoc_id_kind_idx ON elements ((ddoc->>'id_kind')) WHERE ddoc IS NOT NULL;
CREATE INDEX elements_ddoc_gate_idx    ON elements ((ddoc->>'gate_terminal')) WHERE ddoc IS NOT NULL;

CREATE TABLE ddoc_file_refs (            -- the INVERSE index dd asked us for
  id BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY PRIMARY KEY,
  element_id BIGINT NOT NULL REFERENCES elements(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
  target_path TEXT NOT NULL,             -- repo-relative path named by a kind:'file' edge
  rel TEXT NOT NULL,
  location TEXT NOT NULL,                -- JSONPath into the source document
  UNIQUE (element_id, target_path, rel, location)
);
CREATE INDEX ddoc_file_refs_target_idx ON ddoc_file_refs (target_path);
```
